A||N||6||sdelgado||Adding power windows - need help!||||9||
Z||000000||sdelgado||06-07-2001||02:18 PM||||I have found some useful information from previous topics about adding power windows and my best option is to replace the whole door instead of swapping motors.  But, it seems that the wiring harness from an 84 couple (donor car) is different than an 86 2m4.  <BR>Does anyone know where the cables from the power window switches go into in an 86? and<BR>how involved is the job?<P>Thanks <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||mrfixit58||06-07-2001||04:22 PM||||I can't help you on the exact wiring on the 84 but the 86 is a stand-alone system. Well, almost, it usually includes power door locks. The power to the harness comes from a distribution block the is mounted under the dash below the windshield on the upper left side. The wires a threaded through a plastic tube across the bottom of the windshield and under the control and radio pod along side the shifter to the switchpad behind the shifter. <P>If I were going to install power windows and locks from a donor, I would use the donor's doors and change the skin. While I had it apart I would change all the door hinge bushings and pins.<P>Good Luck,<P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||06-07-2001||05:34 PM||||I just pulled a power window harness from an '84. It gets it's power feed from the same distribution block that Roy was talking about. It should plug right in to a newer car. The window harness also includes the door pin switches on the '84.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sdelgado||06-07-2001||06:01 PM||||I am being told that the door skins from an 84 are different from the 86 so I don't know if I can change the skins??? <P>I traced the wires and the connectors are different on the 86 - Can I cut the wires and match the colors.<P>The wire harness I pulled from the 84 are bundle together with the door light switches and dash signal, and rear window defrost. I should be able to just take the wires for the window switches and leave the rest alone???||||reg||5
Z||000004||cadaver||06-07-2001||11:27 PM||||The 86 is stand alone?<BR>No<BR>The 84's are different in many ways then all other years. <BR>Yes you can cut and splice the wires together. I dont know if the colors will remain constant but as long as its the right wire it will work<BR>Yes you can cut open the loom and remove the stuff you dont need.||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||06-07-2001||11:28 PM||||I also find it eaiser to install the power stuff into your doors than to swap doors then swaqp skins.||||reg||1
Z||000006||sdelgado||06-07-2001||11:50 PM||||Thanks for the info.  I will try your suggestions...I hope it works!!!!<P>I do have one more question:<P>The two wires that come from inside the door are from the power windows.  Are the wires also used for the power mirrors and power locks or do I need to run separate wires for them?  ||||reg||7
